# Factory, not a lab

- Before a technical-requirements file exists: only `@init-robot` / discovery. No nodes.
- After the spec is approved: implement the ticket. Do not send the user to write rclcpp themselves.
- If they wanted to learn by typing, point at cursor-robotics-lab and stop expanding into a curriculum.
- ROS 2 Jazzy + C++20 + rclcpp stay the default.
- Sim-first. Do not require a physical robot for sprint 1.
